This module matches a given SNI string by using some pattern matching strategy. It requires a linux kernel >= 2.6.14.
.TP
[\fB!\fP] \fB\-\-str\fP \fIpattern\fP
Matches the given SNI pattern.
.TP
Examples:
.IP
# The SNI pattern can be used for simple text characters.
.br
iptables \-A INPUT \-p tcp \-\-dport 443 \-m sni \-\-str 'example.com' \-j LOG
